the entertainment and sports bookings business that showcase a range of concerts, family shows, and special events, as well as various sporting events. The company was formerly known as MSGE Spinco, Inc. Madison Square Garden Entertainment Corp. was incorporated in 2022 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Lawrence Dolan | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $5.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $305K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $31K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Madison Square Garden Entertain is a mid-cap communication services business with a $3.9B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $323M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.38549528855222165},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Madison Square Garden EVP Philip D'Ambrosio Sells 19,178 MSGE Shares in Late November 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/madison-square-garden-evp-philip-dambrosio-sells-19178-msge-shares-in-late-november-2026","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795642543.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(MSGE) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/MSGE_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_112526043001_1795599001.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795599001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":